── SYNTAX ERROR ─────────────────────────── E0100_python_lambda.lt:1:56  [E0100]

Stilt writes a closure as `|x| x * 2`:

  1 │ fn doubled(xs: List<i64>) -> List<i64> { xs.map(lambda x: x * 2) }
    │                                                        ^

A closure is its parameters between `|`, then its body.

To fix it, write the closure with `|`:

  1 │ fn doubled(xs: List<i64>) -> List<i64> { xs.map(|x| x * 2) }
    │                                                 ~~~
